{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the generations of the sons of Noah: Shem, Ham, and Japheth.</b> From this verse until the section ״ויהי כל הארץ שפה אחת ודברים אחדים״ you will find seventy persons in exact count, all of them generations of Noah. And at the end of the section it is written: ״אלה משפחות בני נח לתולדותם בגוייהם ומאלה נפרדו הגוים בארץ אחר המבול״. From this one may learn that there are seventy nations in the world, and each and every nation has its own language, since this verse comes and teaches that they separated one by one, each man to his language — that is, that each one established for itself its own language. Therefore you will find that the generations in this section number seventy, corresponding to the seventy souls that our forefathers went down to Egypt. And from this the verse says (Deuteronomy 32:8): ״בהנחל עליון גוים בהפרידו בני אדם״. Its meaning: from the time the children of men separated in the world — which is what is written here, ״ומאלה נפרדו״ — from that time ״יצב גבולות עמים״; the Holy One, blessed be He, established seventy nations in the world, למספר בני ישראל — corresponding to the number of those who went down to Egypt, who were seventy souls. And therefore it did not say למספר בני יעקב, for that would have implied the twelve tribes." "<b>And know</b> that all this length that the Scripture extended in the generations of Ham — the intention is to make known to us all the nations that came forth from him, which Abraham, who came forth from the sons of Shem, attained. And because of this the Scripture extended in the generations of Ham and in the generations of Shem, to make known that the intent and the choice do not lie in the seventy nations and in the rest of the generations, but only to bring forth from them the chosen treasure, Abraham and his seed. And our Rabbis of blessed memory already brought a parable for this matter. They said: To what may the matter be compared? To a man who lost a pearl in the sand, and he brings a sieve and sifts all the sand until he finds the pearl; once he has found the pearl, he discards the sand. And the parable comes to say that just as the intention is not with the sand, which is the multitude, but only with the single pearl, so the ultimate intent is not in the multitude of these gentile nations but only in the holy people that comes forth from them — the seed of Abraham. And this is what they said of blessed memory: ״מחשבתן של ישראל קדמה״. And you already know that the beginning of thought is the end of deed. And even though reason testifies to this — that whatever is last in deed was first in thought — it is possible to prove this from Scripture: for we find regarding the labor of the Tabernacle (Exodus 35:35): ״לעשות כל מלאכת חרש וחושב״, and it is written (ibid.): ״ולחשוב מחשבות לעשות בזהב ובכסף ובנחשת״." "<b>And the Ramban wrote</b> that from all these accounts of generations the renewal of the world will be verified for those who hear, for Abraham our father of blessed memory would command his sons and his household after him and would testify to them concerning Noah and his sons who were in the ark. And behold, Abraham of blessed memory, who saw Noah, is a witness by the mouth of a witness regarding the entire matter of the Flood. And he is a third-hand witness regarding the Creation, for Lamech, the father of Noah, saw Adam the first man; and Isaac and Jacob saw Shem, the witness to the Flood. And Jacob related all this to those who went down to Egypt, also to Pharaoh and the people of his generation. And the people in every generation know from their forefathers — four and five generations relate their deeds and their generations — accordingly." "<b>And the sage R. Abraham ibn Ezra of blessed memory wrote</b> that Noah lived until Abraham was fifty-eight years old, and he made a mnemonic sign for this: Abraham our father was fifty-eight years old when Noah died."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:42.809224972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}